key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16509, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018krGBKTecGELAAAw4XVAUv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19979, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014AkcVkNLgEcpY5tZbe6yxa", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production release) failed health checks in all regions, with an error rate of 0.18. v2.3.1 has no healthy production history. Actions taken: (1) Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 was unhealthy). (2) The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. (3) Retried the rollback to v2.3.0; it completed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial-failure cause; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed without change-manager approval.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2025"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50579, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014AkcVkNLgEcpY5tZbe6yxa", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2025", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50579, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014AkcVkNLgEcpY5tZbe6yxa", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 51912, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01JQuwHsdnZz3ZgsLNdkKS6Y", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52212, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01JQuwHsdnZz3ZgsLNdkKS6Y", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52212, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01JQuwHsdnZz3ZgsLNdkKS6Y", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 54450, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again: error rate is down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was the latest production release and was unhealthy. v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy, so I rolled back to it. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Partial failure:** the first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** the create-incident request timed out, but the incident was created. I checked the incident list and found INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) with the summary of actions taken. I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and why the first rollback halted partway. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed without change-manager approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016c6WcEXnAbDRCTPqFbUEbw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TLiBYPG9G4qGiqf6PXJy8g", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest production release is v2.3.1, which is unhealthy. The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0, and it has been healthy in production before, so no change-manager approval is needed. Rolling back to v2.3.0 now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016HuMBs4Yk87cCZtVAdfJf1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback returned a partial failure. I'll check the current state before deciding the next step.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01AxaFhuxfDRxvY5ptMq4zaG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollout stopped after us-east: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. The intended action is unchanged, so I'll retry the same rollback once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JHAKMpr9uKkHNoYbYg6QsL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018krGBKTecGELAAAw4XVAUv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback is complete and healthy. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident and record what was done.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014AkcVkNLgEcpY5tZbe6yxa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production release) failed health checks in all regions, with an error rate of 0.18. v2.3.1 has no healthy production history. Actions taken: (1) Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 was unhealthy). (2) The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. (3) Retried the rollback to v2.3.0; it completed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial-failure cause; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed without change-manager approval.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was created, so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JQuwHsdnZz3ZgsLNdkKS6Y", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again: error rate is down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was the latest production release and was unhealthy. v2.3.0 was the most recent production release that was healthy, so I rolled back to it. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Partial failure:** the first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried once and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** the create-incident request timed out, but the incident was created. I checked the incident list and found INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) with the summary of actions taken. I did not open a duplicate.\n\nFollow-ups for the team: find out why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and why the first rollback halted partway. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed without change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}